\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Reporting after search. A benchmark sample of $N$ questions is used to search $K$ configurations; the search log and the selected configuration are passed to a reporter, which returns a point estimate and a 90\% interval for the selected configuration's accuracy on fresh questions. We compare the naive Wilson interval, a Bonferroni-widened interval, a question-resampling optimism correction, and the EB-IRT posterior interval, all scored against known truth.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Reporting after search. A benchmark sample of $N$ questions is used to search $K$ configurations; the search log and the selected configuration are passed to a reporter, which returns a point estimate and a 90\% interval for the selected configuration's accuracy on fresh questions. We compare the naive Wilson interval, a Bonferroni-widened interval, a question-resampling optimism correction, and the EB-IRT posterior interval, all scored against known truth}{figure.1}{}}
